{"name":"Desert Rose","hex":"#cd616b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert rose","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see desert,‎ rose.","a flowering plant\nA flowering plant of species Adenium obesum, native to Africa and the Middle East; a common ornamental.\nA star rose, gooseberry rose (Rosa stellata), a rose native to North America.\nSturt’s desert rose (Gossypium sturtianum), of Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert_rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adenium","blocks":[{"text":"Adenium is a genus of flowering plants in the family Apocynaceae first described as a genus in 1819. It is native to Africa and the Arabian Peninsula."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Adenium_obesum_%28Forssk.%29_Roemer_%26_Schultes_%282%29.jpg/330px-Adenium_obesum_%28Forssk.%29_Roemer_%26_Schultes_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adenium"},{"title":"Rosa stellata","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa stellata is a species of rose known by the common names desert rose, gooseberry rose, and star rose. In Texas this type of rose grows on dry rocky places to 6,500 feet (2,000 m), such as the Trans-Pecos. It occurs in the mountain canyons of Arizona and New Mexico. It also grows in dry, rocky places. It has trifoliate leaves, deep rose purple blossoms and yellowish white prickles on the petioles and stems. It is a perennial shrub with velvety, deciduous leaves. Some horticulturists consider it to be a browse plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Rosa_stellata_mirifica.jpg/330px-Rosa_stellata_mirifica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_stellata"},{"title":"Desert Rose (Sting song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Desert Rose\" is a song by British musician Sting featuring Algerian raï singer Cheb Mami, from Sting's sixth solo studio album, Brand New Day (1999). According to Sting, the lyrics have to do with \"lost love and longing\". Riding a wave of pre-9/11 interest in Latin and Arabic cultures, \"Desert Rose\" peaked at No. 2 in Canada, No. 3 in Switzerland, No. 4 in Italy, No. 15 in the United Kingdom, and No. 17 in the United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Desert_Rose_%28Sting_song%29_coverart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_Rose_(Sting_song)"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Adenium_africana_seedlings.png/500px-Adenium_africana_seedlings.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Adenium_africana_seedlings.png/1280px-Adenium_africana_seedlings.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Adenium_africana_seedlings.png/500px-Adenium_africana_seedlings.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Seedlings ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdenium_africana_seedlings.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/D85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg/500px-D85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/D85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg/1280px-D85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/D85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg/500px-D85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adenium in Thailand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AD85_0926_Adenium_in_Thailand.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Bursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg/500px-Bursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Bursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg/1280px-Bursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Bursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg/500px-Bursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the paired, follicular fruit of an Adenium species, dehiscing to release seeds equipped with a double pappus (i.e. tuft of hairs at each end) for wind-dispersal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABursted_Adenium_seeds.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Desert_Rose_Adenium.jpg/500px-Desert_Rose_Adenium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe